## Ring topology — project

Every folder in this project belongs to one of six ordinal rings by role. Ring order governs dependency. Inner rings serve outer rings; outer rings never call inward.

```text
R0  Scripts     script/                 automation — run-logged.sh, registry population; serves every ring
R1  Bitacora    _knowledge/_bitacora/   records + tooling — task-todo, task-report, task-stdout;
                                        bitacora-create.sh, bitacora-close.sh, bitacora-find.sh,
                                        bitacora-log.sh; shared substrate
R2  Precept     precept/                governing rules — declarative action-domain files
R3  Concept     concept/                study anchors — topic division, one file per chapter
R4  Reference   reference/              distilled truth — citations with claim mapping
R5  Fixture     fixture/                practice material — compilable per-chapter code
```

Support layers sit outside the ordinal chain:

```text
rings/    mirrored ring-topology specifications — read-only references
skills/   symlinked skill catalog — live links to sources, never stale
```

Ring constraints:

- Scripts serve every ring; bitacora records and logs every ring. Inner rings complete before outer rings advance (precept → concept → reference → fixture).
- Fixture compiles against reference claims; reference distills from concept anchors; concept derives from precept rules.
- Support layers inform the chain; they never govern it.

